## 7b. The Go side

The Go harness is `pekko-actor/actor/judge_internal_test.go`; it writes the event log of section 2 and the verdict is the
same `comparator.py`. Which scenarios it runs, and which clause of a scenario does not apply to Go (with the reason), are
listed in `judge/go-scope.json`; `judge/go_scope.py` rejects a stale or reasonless waiver. `judge/run-go.sh` runs it and
`judge/mutate_go.py` breaks the Go core on a scratch copy to show the judge fails on broken code (section 6, item 3).
Status and limits: [actor-core-parity.md](actor-core-parity.md).

**Restart and supervision scenarios in the Go gate.** S13 (two restarts send no `terminated`, the stop sends one, `DeathWatchSpec.scala:195-211`), S14 (an initialization failure
stops the child) and S16 (a conflicting watch fails the watcher once, an identical repeat does not) are in `scenarios`, with
no waiver. The Go harness records `pre-restart`, `post-restart`, `decided` and the instance number `i` (see the header of
`judge_internal_test.go`), so `I6.a` and `I6.b` are decided on real `decided` events and `G6.d` on real `terminated` events.
`G7.b` has two halves and only one can fire for S14, on either side: a child whose start failed is replaced by the creation path
(`faultCreate` in Go, Pekko's `faultCreate`), which runs no `PreRestart`, so `pre-restart` never appears for it; a wrong decider that
restarts it is detected by the **missing `terminated`** (the run still ends, through the witness on the second instance's `pre-start`).
**Difference from Pekko in S14.** Pekko's child throws in `preStart`; the Go child fails in its **factory** on instance 1 (a panic, which
the runtime reports as an `InitializationError` decided by the parent, the same class as a `PreStart` that returns an error and the
